{{Quote|We need that treaty signed so we can gain access to the fuel reserves here on Malastare. Without it, our armies shall be vulnerable.|Supreme Chancellor Sheev Palpatine, to Doge Nakha Urus|<ref name="Zillo Beast" />}}
'''Malastare''' was a [[Tree|forested]] [[planet]] located in the [[Malastare system]] of the [[Mid Rim Territories|Mid Rim]], situated along the [[Hydian Way]]. Its core was home to large reserves of [[Malastarian fuel]], a [[Poison|toxic]] [[fuel]] found only on Malastare. It was the [[homeworld]] of the [[Dug]] [[species]], though it was represented in the [[Galactic Senate]] by the [[Gran]] species, who had colonized Malastare. [[Ainlee Teem]], the [[senator]] of Malastare, was nominated in the election for [[Supreme Chancellor]] during the [[Invasion of Naboo]]. During the [[Clone Wars]], Malastare was the location of a [[Battle of Malastare|battle]] between the [[Galactic Republic]] and the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] over the planet's fuel reserves. The battle awoke a creature known as the [[Zillo Beast]], which the Republic successfully neutralized, leading the [[Dug Council]] to sign a [[Treaty of Malastare|treaty]] with the Republic allowing them access to their fuel reserves.

==Description==
{{Quote|I hope your bomb has not upset the delicate balance of our planet.|Doge Nakha Urus|<ref name="Zillo Beast" />}}
[[File:MalastareFuelLines-TZB.png|thumb|left|180px|Malastare fuel lines]]
Malastare was located within the [[Star system|system]] of [[Malastare system|the same name]], which occupied the [[Dustig sector]] of the [[Mid Rim Territories|Mid Rim]].<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> The world acted as a junction between the [[Hydian Way]] [[hyperspace route]]&mdash;which connected it to [[ZeHeth]] and [[Darkknell]]<ref name="TFABG" />&mdash;and the [[Biox Detour]], which linked Malastare to the [[Ring of Kafrene]] [[mining]] colony.<ref name="Smuggler's Guide" />

The surface of Malastare was heavily forested,<ref name="Malastare" /> and its core was home to large reserves of [[Malastarian fuel|fuel]]. As a result, the [[Homeworld|native]] [[Dug]]s cleared large portions of land, constructing refineries to extract the [[fuel]] vital to its economy.<ref name="Zillo Beast" /> [[Podracing]] was a popular sport on Malastare.<ref name="Episode I">{{Film|I}}</ref>

==History==
===Early history===
{{Quote|That thing, it is a Zillo Beast. They once roamed Malastare, devouring our ancestors. When the Dugs first started harvesting the fuel in the planet's core, ''they were killed off''. They are supposed to be extinct. Apparently, they're not.|Doge Nakha Urus|<ref name="Zillo Beast" />}}
[[File:Dug_writing.png|300px|thumb|Doge Nakha Urus reads an ancient manuscript detailing the Zillo Beasts.]]
In ancient times, Malastare was plagued by [[Zillo Beast]]s, who feasted on the native Dug population. The creatures were driven to near extinction when it was discovered by the Dugs that Malastarian fuel was toxic to them. However, it was prophesied that one would eventually return, and bring an end to Dug civilization. In order to prepare their descendants, a manuscript detailing the Zillo Beasts was passed down through future generations.<ref name="Zillo Beast" />

In the [[Standard century|centuries]] before the [[Imperial Era]], members of the [[Gran]] [[species]] arrived on Malastare to [[Colonization of Malastare|colonize the world]], only to be met by fierce Dug resistance. In the brutal Gran-Dug war that ensued, the Gran held the technological advantage, whereas the Dugs put a defense with an unrelenting ability and great resourcefulness. In the end, the conflict escalated to such a point that the [[Galactic Republic]] needed to step in and establish a ceasefire. As the Gran colonists held greater influence in the Republic than the native Dugs, the Republic all but gave the world over to the Gran during talks via the [[Gran Protectorate Act]]. Officially, however, the Gran were granted the eastern continent of Malastare, while the Republic moved the Dugs to the planet's western continent.<ref name="Special Mods">''[[Special Modifications]]''</ref>

By the [[High Republic Era]], Malastare had formed the [[Malastare-Sullust Joint Task Force]] alongside<ref name="Light">''[[The High Republic: Light of the Jedi]]''</ref> the world of<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> [[Sullust]], keeping order in their small sector of the Mid Rim against [[pirate]]s and other similar threats. Their joint [[fleet]] included a [[commanding officer]] named [[Hedda Casset]], who served in the task force for over thirty [[Standard year|years]].<ref name="Light" />

===Late Republic Era===
====A falling Republic====
{{Quote|They have podracing on Malastare. Very fast, very dangerous.|[[Qui-Gon Jinn]]|<ref name="Episode I" />}}
Over time, significant Gran and [[human]] populations migrated to Malastare. Podracing became extremely popular on the forested planet,<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> and the [[city]] of [[Pixelito]] was the birthplace of [[Sebulba]], who became one of the most celebrated [[Podracer (profession)|podracers]] in history.<ref name="Episode I" />

During the [[Trade Federation]]'s [[Invasion of Naboo]], Malastare was represented by Gran [[senator]] [[Ainlee Teem]] in the [[Galactic Senate]]. Ainlee was nominated as a candidate to become [[Supreme Chancellor]] after [[Finis Valorum]] was voted out of office through a [[Vote of No Confidence]]. However, senator [[Darth Sidious|Sheev Palpatine]] of Naboo was elected to fill the position instead.<ref name="Episode I" />

At some point, a [[Corporate Alliance]] [[fleet]], led by the brilliant [[Harch]] tactician [[Admiral]] [[Trench]], [[blockade]]d [[Malastare Narrows]]. A dispatched [[Galactic Republic|Republic]] task force led by [[Wullf Yularen]] [[Battle of Malastare Narrows|engaged]] the corporate fleet. Despite taking heavy casualties, reinforcements led by [[Jedi Master]] [[Kep-She]] allowed the blockade to be broken, and it seemingly killed Trench.<ref name="Cat and Mouse" /> Amid the [[Separatist Crisis]], [[Eriadu Mining and Shipping|Eriadu Mining]] shipped [[lommite]] ore though Malastare to the [[Core Worlds]].<ref name="Tarkin">[[Tarkin (novel)|''Tarkin'']]</ref>

====Clone Wars====
[[File:Electro-proton_explosion.png|215x215px|left|thumb|The electro-proton bomb detonates, deactivating the Separatist Droid Army.]]
During the [[Clone Wars]], the [[Grand Army of the Republic]] and [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatist]] [[Separatist Droid Army|Droid Army]] fought a [[Battle of Malastare|battle]] over Malastare's fuel reserves. Supreme Chancellor Palpatine authorized the use of an experimental [[electro-proton bomb]], despite the concerns of [[Doge]] [[Nakha Urus]], the leader of the [[Dug Council]]. The device succeeded in deactivating the Droid Army, while leaving the Republic's [[clone trooper]]s unharmed. However, the explosion opened up a massive [[sinkhole]] in the ground, which swallowed clones and [[droid]]s alike.<ref name="Zillo Beast" />

While the Dug Council gathered to decide whether to sign a [[Treaty of Malastare|treaty]] with the Republic allowing them access to Malastare's fuel reserves, a rescue team led by Jedi Master [[Mace Windu]] descended into the sinkhole to rescue Republic troopers, finding several survivors. However, they found that the bomb had awoken the last surviving Zillo Beast, and barely escaped with their lives. Doge Urus demanded Republic assistance in eliminating the creature, threatening to cancel the treaty if they didn't. Windu declined due to the fact it was innocent and the last of its kind. The Supreme Chancellor and [[Doctor]] [[Sionver Boll]] expressed interest in examining the [[lightsaber]]-resistant plates of the Zillo Beast, believing that they could be used to improve [[armor]] for the clone army.<ref name="Zillo Beast" />

[[File:Zillo_beast_attacks.jpg|255x255px|thumb|The Zillo Beast attacks the Republic and Dug forces.]]
Discovering unprotected gaps between its plates, the Republic utilized [[RX-200 Falchion-class assault tank|RX-200 ''Falchion''-class assault tanks]] to sedate the creature, leading the Dugs to believe it to be [[Death|dead]]. Despite plans to relocate it somewhere in the [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]], Palpatine ordered it to be taken to [[Coruscant]], so it could be studied in a controlled environment. The Malastarian council signed the treaty, granting the Republic access to vital fuel reserves.<ref name="Zillo Beast" />

===Galactic Empire===
{{Quote|Do you want to lose here as you did on Malastare? The loss of that communications station lost us our meager hold on that world.|[[General]] [[Jylia Shale]] to [[Grand Moff]] [[Valco Pandion]]|<ref name="Aftermath" />}}
After the end of the Clone Wars, Malastare fell under the control of the Republic's [[Proclamation of the New Order|successor]], the [[Galactic Empire]]. It notably housed an important [[Malastare communications station|communications station]].<ref name="Aftermath" /> [[Sorbee Manufacturing]] was active on Malastare and produced materiel for military contracts, industrial machines, submersible vehicles, and mining equipment. The company also produced parts for podracing, which continued on Malastare into the [[Imperial Era]].<ref name="Beyond Victory" />

Malastare was intended to be a target of the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance's]] [[61st Mobile Infantry]] during [[Operation Ringbreaker]], but the attack never happened as the operation was called off following the [[siege of Inyusu Tor]].<ref name="Rebel Files">''[[Star Wars: The Rebel Files]]''</ref> Although it was successfully [[Battle of Malastare (Galactic Civil War)|targeted]] by [[Blade Squadron]]<ref name="Insider 160" /> shortly after the [[Battle of Endor]],<ref name="Aftermath" /> the Imperial presence would remain even after the [[Rebellion on Akiva|destruction]] of the [[Imperial Future Council]] on [[Akiva]]. [[Grand General]] [[Kenner Loring]] would choose to [[Entrenchment on Malastare|entrench]] himself on the planet in opposition to [[Fleet Admiral]] [[Gallius Rax]]'s ''de facto'' control of the fragmented Empire.<ref name="LD" />

==Government==
{{Quote|And the Dugs? Have they signed the treaty?''"<br />"''No, Chancellor, the treaty must be passed by the council.|Supreme Chancellor Sheev Palpatine and Doge Nakha Urus|<ref name="Zillo Beast" />}}
[[File:Dug_Council.png|250px|left|thumb|Doge Nakha Urus and several members of the Dug Council]]
Malastare had a government that was considered curious and which reflected the divide between the Gran and Dugs. The internal affairs of Malastare were controlled by the Dug Council, who ruled from the [[Imperial palace (Malastare)|Imperial palace]]. The council had five members<ref name="GuidetoGalaxy">{{BuildFalconCite|64|Guide to the Galaxy}}</ref> and was led by the Doge. The council was able to ratify treaties. During the Clone Wars, it was led by Doge Nakha Urus.<ref name="Zillo Beast" />

However, in the Galactic Senate,<ref name="GuidetoGalaxy" /> the interests of Malastare were solely represented by the Grans.<ref name="Malastare" /> By the time of the Trade Federation's Invasion of Naboo, Malastare was specifically represented via [[Ainlee Teem]].<ref name="GuidetoGalaxy" /> Also present was Senator [[Aks Moe]] and the rest of the [[Congress of Malastare]].<ref name="Episode I" /> At some point, however, at least two Dugs were able to join the Congress and were present in the Galactic Senate alongside Gran representatives.<ref name="Card">{{SWU|set=Secrets of Power|cardname=Congress of Malastare|link=1629192496|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/3yLBy}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
Malastare was first mentioned in the [[1999]] film [[Star Wars: Episode I The Phantom Menace|''Star Wars'': Episode I ''The Phantom Menace'']].<ref name="Episode I" /> It was mentioned again in a deleted scene from [[Star Wars: Episode II Attack of the Clones|''Star Wars'': Episode II ''Attack of the Clones'']], released in [[2002]].<ref name="Episode II">{{Film|II}}</ref> Malastare made its first on-screen appearances in "[[The Zillo Beast]]," an episode from the [[The Clone Wars: Season Two|second season]] of the [[2008]] animated series ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]''.<ref name="Zillo Beast" />

In the initial hardcover and [[The High Republic: The Eye of Darkness (audiobook)|audiobook]] release of ''[[The High Republic: The Eye of Darkness]]'', the list of planets brought under Nihil control by the [[expansion of the Stormwall]] includes Malastare. The digital release edits the list and instead places [[Elrood]] behind the new Stormwall border.<ref name="Post-release edit">{{WordPress|subdomain=numidianprime|url=2023/11/16/the-occlusion-zone-of-the-nihil-2|name=Numidian Prime|text=The Occlusion Zone of the Nihil|archivedate=20231201060644}}</ref>

